# Anchored to the repo root on purpose. Unanchored `logs/` also matched
# `results/b7/logs/`, and git does not descend into an ignored directory, so no
# later negation could have rescued those files -- the run artifacts would have
# been silently dropped at commit time.
/logs/
/outputs/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.jsonl
!probe_pipeline/pairs/*.jsonl
!rm_channel/prompts/*.jsonl
# results/ is the curated, committed record of completed runs. It previously
# needed `git add -f` to get past the blanket rule above, which is easy to
# forget and silently loses artifacts.
!results/**/*.jsonl
.env
*.egg-info/
